<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρι-έσπερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑσπέρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>in three successive nights,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνειρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Somn.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gall.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. λέων,</span> i. e. Heracles, <i>who
				was begotten in a triple night,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				33
			</span></i>; Subst., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἡρακλέους τ.</span>”
				<i>the triple night,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.38
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
